{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-124676",
  "enisaUuid": "188459a1-2f75-386a-b0d4-e4ec6f36c6c3",
  "description": "A flaw was found in Foreman\u2019s Api::V2::MailNotificationsController, where authorization checks on user-specific mail-notification resources are insufficient. The GET /api/v2/users/:id/mail_notifications endpoint resolves the target account using User.find(params[:id]) without verifying that the authenticated user is authorized to access that user\u2019s notification configuration. Additionally, the POST and PUT /api/v2/users/:user_id/mail_notifications paths call deny_access when the requester is unauthorized but fail to halt execution, allowing the request to continue and persist the unauthorized change despite a 403 response or subsequent DoubleRenderError. This can allow a user to disclose another user\u2019s mail-notification configuration, including mail_query values, and, where write permissions apply, modify or create notification settings for another user.",
